  "body": "Refs #566\nDirect-PR: one-line follow-up of #575 (Fable finding 6)\nClaim: ext/francoisgn-bug-566\n\n## Problem\nFable finding 6, non-blocking, on #575 (https://github.com/ezzz/HFRnow/pull/575#issuecomment-6709646711): in `FilteredPostsView`, the `failed:` closure kept `readyToken`.\nWhen an already-shown page crashes and its reload then fails twice, the `failed` flag is set. The \"Réessayer\" view only appears while `readyToken == nil`, so the user sees a blank web view and no \"Réessayer\".\n\n## Change\nThe `failed:` closure now sets `readyToken = nil` before `failed = true`. This is the same rule `TopicReaderModel.documentDidFail` follows since #575.\n\n## Tests\nNone added. `readyToken` and `failed` are private `@State` of the view, and the app has no view-test harness for them. The reader-side equivalent is covered by `aFailureOfADocumentReadyEarlierIsStillAnError`.\n\n`swiftlint --strict` reports 0 violations. Fable said its APPROVE on #575 carries over to exactly this change.\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code/session_014QH2CGQsLP81KmFzQPsMzc)_\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai -->\n\n<!-- coderabbit-ai-generated:v1 -->\n\n## Summary by CodeRabbit\n\n* **Bug Fixes**\n  * Corrected the view’s state when the current document fails to load. It is no longer left marked as ready after a failure, so the displayed status reflects the error. Failures from outdated documents continue to be ignored.\n\n<!-- end of auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai -->",
